["<aside class=\"callout why\"><div class=\"callout-t\">Why it matters</div><p>Be on the glass when the bear is on the food. This chapter is the clock, and how weather and people bend it.</p></aside><figure class=\"diagram\"><svg xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/2000/svg\" viewBox=\"0 0 400 300\" font-family=\"sans-serif\" role=\"img\" aria-label=\"24 hour clock of a typical fall black bear day. Feeding peaks at dawn and dusk, shown in orange, about 6 to 8:30 in the morning and 4:30 to 7:30 in the evening. Through the day it feeds and beds in shade, shown in sage. Night is mostly rest, but near people bears feed more at night. Times are typical, not exact.\">\n<rect x=\"0\" y=\"0\" width=\"400\" height=\"300\" fill=\"#fffaf0\"/>\n<text x=\"200\" y=\"24\" font-size=\"17\" font-weight=\"bold\" fill=\"#23261f\" text-anchor=\"middle\">A fall bear day (typical)</text><circle cx=\"200\" cy=\"156\" r=\"100\" fill=\"#dfe6d3\"/><path d=\"M107.6 117.7 A100 100 0 0 1 300.0 156.0 L270.0 156.0 A70 70 0 0 0 135.3 129.2 Z\" fill=\"#3d4a5c\"/><path d=\"M300.0 156.0 A100 100 0 0 1 279.3 216.9 L255.5 198.6 A70 70 0 0 0 270.0 156.0 Z\" fill=\"#e8590c\"/><path d=\"M279.3 216.9 A100 100 0 0 1 107.6 194.3 L135.3 182.8 A70 70 0 0 0 255.5 198.6 Z\" fill=\"#8a9a6b\"/><path d=\"M107.6 194.3 A100 100 0 0 1 107.6 117.7 L135.3 129.2 A70 70 0 0 0 135.3 182.8 Z\" fill=\"#e8590c\"/><text x=\"200.0\" y=\"47.0\" font-size=\"14\" font-weight=\"bold\" fill=\"#23261f\" text-anchor=\"middle\">0</text><text x=\"280.61017305526644\" y=\"80.38982694473358\" font-size=\"14\" font-weight=\"bold\" fill=\"#23261f\" text-anchor=\"middle\">3</text><text x=\"314.0\" y=\"161.0\" font-size=\"14\" font-weight=\"bold\" fill=\"#23261f\" text-anchor=\"middle\">6</text><text x=\"280.61017305526644\" y=\"241.61017305526642\" font-size=\"14\" font-weight=\"bold\" fill=\"#23261f\" text-anchor=\"middle\">9</text><text x=\"200.0\" y=\"275.0\" font-size=\"14\" font-weight=\"bold\" fill=\"#23261f\" text-anchor=\"middle\">12</text><text x=\"119.38982694473358\" y=\"241.61017305526644\" font-size=\"14\" font-weight=\"bold\" fill=\"#23261f\" text-anchor=\"middle\">15</text><text x=\"86.0\" y=\"161.0\" font-size=\"14\" font-weight=\"bold\" fill=\"#23261f\" text-anchor=\"middle\">18</text><text x=\"119.38982694473357\" y=\"80.38982694473358\" font-size=\"14\" font-weight=\"bold\" fill=\"#23261f\" text-anchor=\"middle\">21</text><circle cx=\"200\" cy=\"156\" r=\"70\" fill=\"#fffaf0\"/><text x=\"200\" y=\"132\" font-size=\"14\" fill=\"#23261f\" text-anchor=\"middle\">Orange: feeding</text><text x=\"200\" y=\"149\" font-size=\"14\" fill=\"#23261f\" text-anchor=\"middle\">peaks dawn, dusk</text><text x=\"200\" y=\"166\" font-size=\"14\" fill=\"#23261f\" text-anchor=\"middle\">Sage: feeds</text><text x=\"200\" y=\"183\" font-size=\"14\" fill=\"#23261f\" text-anchor=\"middle\">and beds in shade</text><text x=\"200\" y=\"294\" font-size=\"14\" font-weight=\"bold\" fill=\"#2f3a2b\" text-anchor=\"middle\">Near people: more feeding at night (75%)</text>\n</svg>\n</figure><ul><li>Mainly daytime, with dawn and dusk peaks (65 to 75%).</li><li>Near people, more at night <span class=\"cert c-lo\" title=\"Certainty\">75%</span>.</li></ul><details class=\"more\"><summary>More: what this chapter covers</summary><ul><li>Feed, bed and water through a day; dawn and dusk; heat, rain, wind, cold and snow, the moon, and hunting pressure; each with how sure we are.</li><li>Evidence levels: a % means a source; Tip means hunter experience; <span class=\"verify\">VERIFY</span> means no good data found.</li><li>Previous: <a href=\"#/s/mc-black-bear-05\">Chapter 5, The year</a>. Next: <a href=\"#/s/mc-black-bear-07\">Chapter 7, Where they are</a>.</li></ul></details>","<figure class=\"diagram\"><svg xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/2000/svg\" viewBox=\"0 0 400 300\" font-family=\"sans-serif\" role=\"img\" aria-label=\"Cross section of black bear country from creek to ridge. Creek bottom: fish where they run, shrubs and berries. Grassy south facing slope: first green food in spring. Cutblock: berries in summer and fall. Timber: beds and cover next to the food. Avalanche chute higher up: spring and summer greens. From the BC account: spring meadows, riparian, skunk cabbage, avalanche chutes, grassy south slopes, burns.\">\n<rect x=\"0\" y=\"0\" width=\"400\" height=\"300\" fill=\"#fffaf0\"/>\n<text x=\"200\" y=\"24\" font-size=\"17\" font-weight=\"bold\" fill=\"#23261f\" text-anchor=\"middle\">Bear country in one slice</text><path d=\"M0 260 L60 250 L120 200 L190 150 L250 110 L310 70 L360 50 L400 45 L400 300 L0 300 Z\" fill=\"#dfe6d3\"/><path d=\"M0 262 Q40 258 80 262 L80 300 L0 300 Z\" fill=\"#4a7fb0\" opacity=\".7\"/><g transform=\"translate(250 110) scale(0.6)\"><polygon points=\"0,-60 -18,0 18,0\" fill=\"#2f3a2b\"/><rect x=\"-3\" y=\"0\" width=\"6\" height=\"10\" fill=\"#6b4f35\"/></g><g transform=\"translate(270 100) scale(0.7)\"><polygon points=\"0,-60 -18,0 18,0\" fill=\"#2f3a2b\"/><rect x=\"-3\" y=\"0\" width=\"6\" height=\"10\" fill=\"#6b4f35\"/></g><g transform=\"translate(290 88) scale(0.6)\"><polygon points=\"0,-60 -18,0 18,0\" fill=\"#2f3a2b\"/><rect x=\"-3\" y=\"0\" width=\"6\" height=\"10\" fill=\"#6b4f35\"/></g><g transform=\"translate(230 128) scale(0.5)\"><polygon points=\"0,-60 -18,0 18,0\" fill=\"#2f3a2b\"/><rect x=\"-3\" y=\"0\" width=\"6\" height=\"10\" fill=\"#6b4f35\"/></g><g transform=\"translate(150 180) scale(0.8)\"><ellipse cx=\"0\" cy=\"0\" rx=\"26\" ry=\"16\" fill=\"#8a9a6b\"/><circle cx=\"-12\" cy=\"-4\" r=\"2.6\" fill=\"#e8590c\"/><circle cx=\"-2\" cy=\"-9\" r=\"2.6\" fill=\"#e8590c\"/><circle cx=\"8\" cy=\"-2\" r=\"2.6\" fill=\"#e8590c\"/><circle cx=\"14\" cy=\"-8\" r=\"2.6\" fill=\"#e8590c\"/><circle cx=\"-16\" cy=\"4\" r=\"2.6\" fill=\"#e8590c\"/><circle cx=\"4\" cy=\"5\" r=\"2.6\" fill=\"#e8590c\"/></g><g transform=\"translate(185 158) scale(0.8)\"><ellipse cx=\"0\" cy=\"0\" rx=\"26\" ry=\"16\" fill=\"#8a9a6b\"/><circle cx=\"-12\" cy=\"-4\" r=\"2.6\" fill=\"#e8590c\"/><circle cx=\"-2\" cy=\"-9\" r=\"2.6\" fill=\"#e8590c\"/><circle cx=\"8\" cy=\"-2\" r=\"2.6\" fill=\"#e8590c\"/><circle cx=\"14\" cy=\"-8\" r=\"2.6\" fill=\"#e8590c\"/><circle cx=\"-16\" cy=\"4\" r=\"2.6\" fill=\"#e8590c\"/><circle cx=\"4\" cy=\"5\" r=\"2.6\" fill=\"#e8590c\"/></g><path d=\"M335 55 L345 52 L360 130 L345 130 Z\" fill=\"#8a9a6b\"/><text x=\"40\" y=\"284\" font-size=\"14\" font-weight=\"bold\" fill=\"#fff\" text-anchor=\"middle\">Creek</text><text x=\"95\" y=\"240\" font-size=\"14\" font-weight=\"bold\" fill=\"#2f3a2b\" text-anchor=\"middle\">Grassy south slope</text><text x=\"150\" y=\"132\" font-size=\"14\" font-weight=\"bold\" fill=\"#e8590c\" text-anchor=\"middle\">Cutblock berries</text><text x=\"318\" y=\"150\" font-size=\"14\" font-weight=\"bold\" fill=\"#2f3a2b\" text-anchor=\"middle\">Timber: beds</text><text x=\"290\" y=\"46\" font-size=\"14\" font-weight=\"bold\" fill=\"#2f3a2b\" text-anchor=\"middle\">Avalanche chute</text><text x=\"250\" y=\"282\" font-size=\"14\" font-weight=\"bold\" fill=\"#23261f\" text-anchor=\"middle\">Spring low, summer up, fall berries, fish</text>\n</svg>\n</figure><ul><li>Feeds, then beds in cover close by (Tip).</li><li>Travels in cover between food sites <span class=\"cert c-mid\" title=\"Certainty\">90%</span>.</li></ul><details class=\"more\"><summary>More: the daily loop in detail</summary><ul><li>Home ranges are \"several feeding areas connected by travel routes... often located in wooded areas that provide cover\" (90%, BC account).</li><li>Day beds: shallow scrapes in thick cover or at the base of a big tree near food (Tip, chapter 8).</li><li>Hot days: water and shade in creek bottoms (Tip, quick lesson).</li><li>In hyperphagia a bear may forage up to about 20 hours a day (65%, agency and news reports); feeding stretches into midday in cool fall weather (Tip).</li></ul></details>","<figure class=\"diagram\"><svg xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/2000/svg\" viewBox=\"0 0 400 300\" font-family=\"sans-serif\" role=\"img\" aria-label=\"24 hour clock of a typical fall black bear day. Feeding peaks at dawn and dusk, shown in orange, about 6 to 8:30 in the morning and 4:30 to 7:30 in the evening. Through the day it feeds and beds in shade, shown in sage. Night is mostly rest, but near people bears feed more at night. Times are typical, not exact.\">\n<rect x=\"0\" y=\"0\" width=\"400\" height=\"300\" fill=\"#fffaf0\"/>\n<text x=\"200\" y=\"24\" font-size=\"17\" font-weight=\"bold\" fill=\"#23261f\" text-anchor=\"middle\">A fall bear day (typical)</text><circle cx=\"200\" cy=\"156\" r=\"100\" fill=\"#dfe6d3\"/><path d=\"M107.6 117.7 A100 100 0 0 1 300.0 156.0 L270.0 156.0 A70 70 0 0 0 135.3 129.2 Z\" fill=\"#3d4a5c\"/><path d=\"M300.0 156.0 A100 100 0 0 1 279.3 216.9 L255.5 198.6 A70 70 0 0 0 270.0 156.0 Z\" fill=\"#e8590c\"/><path d=\"M279.3 216.9 A100 100 0 0 1 107.6 194.3 L135.3 182.8 A70 70 0 0 0 255.5 198.6 Z\" fill=\"#8a9a6b\"/><path d=\"M107.6 194.3 A100 100 0 0 1 107.6 117.7 L135.3 129.2 A70 70 0 0 0 135.3 182.8 Z\" fill=\"#e8590c\"/><text x=\"200.0\" y=\"47.0\" font-size=\"14\" font-weight=\"bold\" fill=\"#23261f\" text-anchor=\"middle\">0</text><text x=\"280.61017305526644\" y=\"80.38982694473358\" font-size=\"14\" font-weight=\"bold\" fill=\"#23261f\" text-anchor=\"middle\">3</text><text x=\"314.0\" y=\"161.0\" font-size=\"14\" font-weight=\"bold\" fill=\"#23261f\" text-anchor=\"middle\">6</text><text x=\"280.61017305526644\" y=\"241.61017305526642\" font-size=\"14\" font-weight=\"bold\" fill=\"#23261f\" text-anchor=\"middle\">9</text><text x=\"200.0\" y=\"275.0\" font-size=\"14\" font-weight=\"bold\" fill=\"#23261f\" text-anchor=\"middle\">12</text><text x=\"119.38982694473358\" y=\"241.61017305526644\" font-size=\"14\" font-weight=\"bold\" fill=\"#23261f\" text-anchor=\"middle\">15</text><text x=\"86.0\" y=\"161.0\" font-size=\"14\" font-weight=\"bold\" fill=\"#23261f\" text-anchor=\"middle\">18</text><text x=\"119.38982694473357\" y=\"80.38982694473358\" font-size=\"14\" font-weight=\"bold\" fill=\"#23261f\" text-anchor=\"middle\">21</text><circle cx=\"200\" cy=\"156\" r=\"70\" fill=\"#fffaf0\"/><text x=\"200\" y=\"132\" font-size=\"14\" fill=\"#23261f\" text-anchor=\"middle\">Orange: feeding</text><text x=\"200\" y=\"149\" font-size=\"14\" fill=\"#23261f\" text-anchor=\"middle\">peaks dawn, dusk</text><text x=\"200\" y=\"166\" font-size=\"14\" fill=\"#23261f\" text-anchor=\"middle\">Sage: feeds</text><text x=\"200\" y=\"183\" font-size=\"14\" fill=\"#23261f\" text-anchor=\"middle\">and beds in shade</text><text x=\"200\" y=\"294\" font-size=\"14\" font-weight=\"bold\" fill=\"#2f3a2b\" text-anchor=\"middle\">Near people: more feeding at night (75%)</text>\n</svg>\n</figure><ul><li>WildSafeBC: \"mainly diurnal\" <span class=\"cert c-lo\" title=\"Certainty\">75%</span>.</li></ul><ul><li>Glass the first and last 2 hours hardest (Tip).</li></ul><details class=\"more\"><summary>More: timing with evidence</summary><div class=\"tbl\"><table><thead><tr><th>Claim</th><th>Evidence</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td>Mainly active by day</td><td>75%, WildSafeBC</td></tr><tr><td>Dawn and dusk peaks</td><td>70%, quick lesson and BearWise</td></tr><tr><td>Shifts to night near people</td><td>75%, WildSafeBC; 65%, Massachusetts GPS (Global Positioning System) study of 86 bears</td></tr><tr><td>Feeds most of the day in fall</td><td>65%, hyperphagia reports</td></tr><tr><td>Big boars use the last light</td><td>Tip</td></tr></tbody></table></div><aside class=\"callout warn\"><div class=\"callout-t\">Warning</div><p>Study aid only. The official regulations are the law.</p></aside><ul><li>Legal hours for bear: 1 hour before sunrise to 1 hour after sunset (99%, page 11, <a href=\"#/s/rb-legal-methods\">legal methods</a>). No lights, no infrared optics <span class=\"cert c-hi\" title=\"Certainty\">99%</span>.</li></ul></details>","<div class=\"regs\" data-regs=\"r3bear\"></div>","<figure class=\"diagram\"><svg xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/2000/svg\" viewBox=\"0 0 400 300\" font-family=\"sans-serif\" role=\"img\" aria-label=\"Weather and black bears, with how sure we are. Hot afternoon: beds in shade near water, tip. Cool cloudy day: feeds longer in daylight, tip. Rain: keeps feeding and you move quieter, tip. Hard wind: its nose and ears are less sure, tip. First real cold and snow: nudges bears toward the den, 70 percent. Moon: no good bear data found, VERIFY.\">\n<rect x=\"0\" y=\"0\" width=\"400\" height=\"300\" fill=\"#fffaf0\"/>\n<rect x=\"8\" y=\"8\" width=\"384\" height=\"34\" rx=\"8\" fill=\"#2f3a2b\"/><text x=\"20\" y=\"31\" font-size=\"16\" font-weight=\"bold\" fill=\"#fff\" text-anchor=\"start\">Weather and bears: how sure?</text><rect x=\"10\" y=\"50\" width=\"380\" height=\"34\" rx=\"8\" fill=\"#fffaf0\" stroke=\"#8a9a6b\" stroke-width=\"1.5\"/><text x=\"18\" y=\"72\" font-size=\"14\" font-weight=\"bold\" fill=\"#23261f\" text-anchor=\"start\">Hot afternoon</text><text x=\"150\" y=\"72\" font-size=\"14\" fill=\"#23261f\" text-anchor=\"start\">Shade, near water</text><rect x=\"326\" y=\"56\" width=\"58\" height=\"22\" rx=\"11\" fill=\"#8a9a6b\"/><text x=\"355\" y=\"72\" font-size=\"14\" font-weight=\"bold\" fill=\"#fff\" text-anchor=\"middle\">Tip</text><rect x=\"10\" y=\"90\" width=\"380\" height=\"34\" rx=\"8\" fill=\"#fffaf0\" stroke=\"#8a9a6b\" stroke-width=\"1.5\"/><text x=\"18\" y=\"112\" font-size=\"14\" font-weight=\"bold\" fill=\"#23261f\" text-anchor=\"start\">Cool, cloudy</text><text x=\"150\" y=\"112\" font-size=\"14\" fill=\"#23261f\" text-anchor=\"start\">Feeds longer</text><rect x=\"326\" y=\"96\" width=\"58\" height=\"22\" rx=\"11\" fill=\"#8a9a6b\"/><text x=\"355\" y=\"112\" font-size=\"14\" font-weight=\"bold\" fill=\"#fff\" text-anchor=\"middle\">Tip</text><rect x=\"10\" y=\"130\" width=\"380\" height=\"34\" rx=\"8\" fill=\"#fffaf0\" stroke=\"#8a9a6b\" stroke-width=\"1.5\"/><text x=\"18\" y=\"152\" font-size=\"14\" font-weight=\"bold\" fill=\"#23261f\" text-anchor=\"start\">Rain</text><text x=\"150\" y=\"152\" font-size=\"14\" fill=\"#23261f\" text-anchor=\"start\">Keeps feeding</text><rect x=\"326\" y=\"136\" width=\"58\" height=\"22\" rx=\"11\" fill=\"#8a9a6b\"/><text x=\"355\" y=\"152\" font-size=\"14\" font-weight=\"bold\" fill=\"#fff\" text-anchor=\"middle\">Tip</text><rect x=\"10\" y=\"170\" width=\"380\" height=\"34\" rx=\"8\" fill=\"#fffaf0\" stroke=\"#8a9a6b\" stroke-width=\"1.5\"/><text x=\"18\" y=\"192\" font-size=\"14\" font-weight=\"bold\" fill=\"#23261f\" text-anchor=\"start\">Hard wind</text><text x=\"150\" y=\"192\" font-size=\"14\" fill=\"#23261f\" text-anchor=\"start\">Senses less sure</text><rect x=\"326\" y=\"176\" width=\"58\" height=\"22\" rx=\"11\" fill=\"#8a9a6b\"/><text x=\"355\" y=\"192\" font-size=\"14\" font-weight=\"bold\" fill=\"#fff\" text-anchor=\"middle\">Tip</text><rect x=\"10\" y=\"210\" width=\"380\" height=\"34\" rx=\"8\" fill=\"#fffaf0\" stroke=\"#8a9a6b\" stroke-width=\"1.5\"/><text x=\"18\" y=\"232\" font-size=\"14\" font-weight=\"bold\" fill=\"#23261f\" text-anchor=\"start\">First cold, snow</text><text x=\"150\" y=\"232\" font-size=\"14\" fill=\"#23261f\" text-anchor=\"start\">Nudges to den</text><rect x=\"326\" y=\"216\" width=\"58\" height=\"22\" rx=\"11\" fill=\"#2f3a2b\"/><text x=\"355\" y=\"232\" font-size=\"14\" font-weight=\"bold\" fill=\"#fff\" text-anchor=\"middle\">70%</text><rect x=\"10\" y=\"250\" width=\"380\" height=\"34\" rx=\"8\" fill=\"#fffaf0\" stroke=\"#8a9a6b\" stroke-width=\"1.5\"/><text x=\"18\" y=\"272\" font-size=\"14\" font-weight=\"bold\" fill=\"#23261f\" text-anchor=\"start\">Moon</text><text x=\"150\" y=\"272\" font-size=\"14\" fill=\"#23261f\" text-anchor=\"start\">No bear data</text><rect x=\"326\" y=\"256\" width=\"58\" height=\"22\" rx=\"11\" fill=\"#e8590c\"/><text x=\"355\" y=\"272\" font-size=\"13\" font-weight=\"bold\" fill=\"#fff\" text-anchor=\"middle\">VERIFY</text>\n</svg>\n</figure><ul><li>Most weather effects are hunter experience, not studies (Tip).</li></ul><ul><li>No good bear data on the moon: <span class=\"verify\">VERIFY</span>.</li></ul><details class=\"more\"><summary>More: weather in detail</summary><ul><li>Heat: bears bed in shade and near water on hot afternoons (Tip). Early fall heat pushes feeding to dawn and dusk (Tip).</li><li>Cool, cloudy days: longer daylight feeding (Tip).</li><li>Rain: feeding continues; wet ground lets you move quietly (Tip).</li><li>Wind: hard gusts swirl scent and noise; hunt sheltered slopes (Tip, <a href=\"#/s/wind-mastery\">wind mastery</a>).</li><li>Cold weather makes bears \"increasingly lethargic\" before denning (90%, BC account). A first heavy snow as the den trigger is common hunter belief (Tip).</li><li>Barometric pressure and the moon: no bear studies found (<span class=\"verify\">VERIFY</span>). For deer, no moon effect was found (70%, <a href=\"#/s/mc-mule-deer-06\">mule deer chapter 6</a>).</li></ul></details>","<figure class=\"diagram anim\"><svg xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/2000/svg\" viewBox=\"0 0 400 300\" font-family=\"sans-serif\" role=\"img\" aria-label=\"Animation of one day on a slope. The sun rises and crosses the sky. In the morning the sun warms the slope and blue arrows show air rising uphill. Near sunset the air swirls as the thermals switch. In the evening the slope cools and the arrows flow downhill. Morning: be above the deer. Evening: be below.\"><rect width=\"400\" height=\"300\" fill=\"#fdf1d6\"><animate attributeName=\"fill\" values=\"#fdf1d6;#fffaf0;#e9dfcf\" dur=\"9s\" fill=\"freeze\"/></rect><g><circle r=\"16\" fill=\"#e8590c\"/><animateMotion dur=\"9s\" fill=\"freeze\" keyPoints=\"0;0.8;1\" keyTimes=\"0;0.4;1\" calcMode=\"linear\" path=\"M40 150 Q 200 -40 380 150\"/><animate attributeName=\"opacity\" values=\"1;1;0.5\" keyTimes=\"0;0.7;1\" dur=\"9s\" fill=\"freeze\"/></g><path d=\"M0 270 L300 90 L400 90 L400 300 L0 300 Z\" fill=\"#8a9a6b\"/><g fill=\"#2f3a2b\"><polygon points=\"320,90 330,60 340,90\"/><polygon points=\"350,90 360,56 370,90\"/></g><g opacity=\"1\"><animate attributeName=\"opacity\" values=\"1;1;0;0\" keyTimes=\"0;0.31;0.33;1\" dur=\"9s\" fill=\"freeze\"/><g><path d=\"M27.7 225.4 L68.8 200.7 M61.6 212.0 L68.8 200.7 L55.4 201.8\" stroke=\"#4a7fb0\" stroke-width=\"4\" fill=\"none\" stroke-linecap=\"round\" stroke-linejoin=\"round\"/><path d=\"M117.7 171.4 L158.8 146.7 M151.6 158.0 L158.8 146.7 L145.4 147.8\" stroke=\"#4a7fb0\" stroke-width=\"4\" fill=\"none\" stroke-linecap=\"round\" stroke-linejoin=\"round\"/><path d=\"M207.7 117.4 L248.8 92.7 M241.6 104.0 L248.8 92.7 L235.4 93.8\" stroke=\"#4a7fb0\" stroke-width=\"4\" fill=\"none\" stroke-linecap=\"round\" stroke-linejoin=\"round\"/><animateTransform attributeName=\"transform\" type=\"translate\" values=\"0 0;22.3 -13.4\" dur=\"1.5s\" repeatCount=\"indefinite\"/></g><text x=\"12\" y=\"30\" font-size=\"16\" font-weight=\"bold\" fill=\"#2f3a2b\" text-anchor=\"start\">Morning: sun warms the slope</text><text x=\"12\" y=\"52\" font-size=\"16\" font-weight=\"bold\" fill=\"#4a7fb0\" text-anchor=\"start\">Air rises UPHILL</text></g><g opacity=\"0\"><animate attributeName=\"opacity\" values=\"0;0;1;1;0;0\" keyTimes=\"0;0.31;0.33;0.65;0.67;1\" dur=\"9s\" fill=\"freeze\"/><g stroke=\"#4a7fb0\" stroke-width=\"4\" fill=\"none\" stroke-linecap=\"round\"><path d=\"M90 200 c 20 -30, 50 -10, 30 10 c -15 15, -30 -5, -15 -15\"/><path d=\"M200 140 c -20 -30, -50 -10, -30 10 c 15 15, 30 -5, 15 -15\"/></g><text x=\"12\" y=\"30\" font-size=\"16\" font-weight=\"bold\" fill=\"#2f3a2b\" text-anchor=\"start\">Near sunset: the switch</text><text x=\"12\" y=\"52\" font-size=\"16\" font-weight=\"bold\" fill=\"#4a7fb0\" text-anchor=\"start\">Air swirls, mixed</text></g><g opacity=\"0\"><animate attributeName=\"opacity\" values=\"0;0;1;1\" keyTimes=\"0;0.65;0.67;1\" dur=\"9s\" fill=\"freeze\"/><g><path d=\"M68.8 200.7 L27.7 225.4 M41.0 224.4 L27.7 225.4 L34.9 214.1\" stroke=\"#4a7fb0\" stroke-width=\"4\" fill=\"none\" stroke-linecap=\"round\" stroke-linejoin=\"round\"/><path d=\"M158.8 146.7 L117.7 171.4 M131.0 170.4 L117.7 171.4 L124.9 160.1\" stroke=\"#4a7fb0\" stroke-width=\"4\" fill=\"none\" stroke-linecap=\"round\" stroke-linejoin=\"round\"/><path d=\"M248.8 92.7 L207.7 117.4 M221.0 116.4 L207.7 117.4 L214.9 106.1\" stroke=\"#4a7fb0\" stroke-width=\"4\" fill=\"none\" stroke-linecap=\"round\" stroke-linejoin=\"round\"/><animateTransform attributeName=\"transform\" type=\"translate\" values=\"0 0;-22.3 13.4\" dur=\"1.5s\" repeatCount=\"indefinite\"/></g><text x=\"12\" y=\"30\" font-size=\"16\" font-weight=\"bold\" fill=\"#2f3a2b\" text-anchor=\"start\">Evening: slope cools</text><text x=\"12\" y=\"52\" font-size=\"16\" font-weight=\"bold\" fill=\"#4a7fb0\" text-anchor=\"start\">Air sinks DOWNHILL</text></g><g opacity=\"0\"><animate attributeName=\"opacity\" values=\"0;0;1;1\" keyTimes=\"0;0.65;0.67;1\" dur=\"9s\" fill=\"freeze\"/><rect x=\"190\" y=\"230\" width=\"200\" height=\"56\" rx=\"8\" fill=\"#2f3a2b\"/><text x=\"290\" y=\"254\" font-size=\"14\" font-weight=\"bold\" fill=\"#fff\" text-anchor=\"middle\">Morning: be above</text><text x=\"290\" y=\"274\" font-size=\"14\" font-weight=\"bold\" fill=\"#fff\" text-anchor=\"middle\">Evening: be below</text></g></svg>\n<figcaption>The day's air: up in the morning, down at night. <button class=\"anim-replay\">↻ Replay</button></figcaption></figure>","<figure class=\"diagram anim\"><svg xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/2000/svg\" viewBox=\"0 0 400 342\" font-family=\"sans-serif\" role=\"img\" aria-label=\"Animation: a black bear feeds, head down, in a berry patch on the slope above you. At first the wind blows from the bear toward you, so your scent cone trails behind you, downhill, away from the bear: good. Then the wind swings around and your scent cone swings and stretches up toward the bear. The bear lifts its head: it smells you. Your scent rides the wind; check the wind before every move.\">\n<rect width=\"400\" height=\"342\" fill=\"#fffaf0\"/>\n<defs><linearGradient id=\"mc-black-bear-sc