t-cone-cone)\"/><animateTransform attributeName=\"transform\" type=\"scale\" values=\"1;1;2.1;2.1\" keyTimes=\"0;0.55;0.8;1\" dur=\"7s\" fill=\"freeze\"/></g><animateTransform attributeName=\"transform\" type=\"rotate\" values=\"0;0;180;180\" keyTimes=\"0;0.55;0.8;1\" dur=\"7s\" fill=\"freeze\"/></g></g>\n<ellipse cx=\"200\" cy=\"142\" rx=\"56\" ry=\"6\" fill=\"#9fae7e\" opacity=\".8\"/>\n<path d=\"M150 112 C148 92 162 82 184 82 C204 80 222 84 236 92 C246 98 250 108 248 118 L246 138 L238 140 L234 122 C226 126 214 126 206 124 L204 140 L196 141 L194 124 C182 124 172 124 166 122 L164 140 L156 141 L154 122 C150 120 150 116 150 112z\" fill=\"#1f1d1a\" stroke=\"#0e0d0b\" stroke-width=\"1.2\"/>\n<g><path d=\"M236 96 C246 88 258 88 266 94 L280 100 C286 102 286 108 280 110 L266 112 C258 116 246 114 240 108z\" fill=\"#1f1d1a\"/><path d=\"M268 96 L281 100 C286 102 286 108 280 110 L268 109z\" fill=\"#8b6a4a\"/><circle cx=\"283\" cy=\"104\" r=\"2\" fill=\"#0e0d0b\"/><circle cx=\"246\" cy=\"88\" r=\"5.5\" fill=\"#1f1d1a\"/><circle cx=\"262\" cy=\"98\" r=\"1.8\" fill=\"#eee\"/><animateTransform attributeName=\"transform\" type=\"rotate\" values=\"22 238 100;22 238 100;-8 238 100\" keyTimes=\"0;0.9;1\" begin=\"0s\" dur=\"6s\" fill=\"freeze\"/></g>\n<text x=\"200\" y=\"76\" font-size=\"15\" font-weight=\"bold\" fill=\"#2f3a2b\" text-anchor=\"middle\">bear</text>\n<g transform=\"translate(200 236)\"><circle cx=\"0\" cy=\"-16\" r=\"6\" fill=\"#e0b48c\"/><path d=\"M-8 -9 h16 l2 18 h-20z\" fill=\"#e8590c\"/><path d=\"M-5 9 v14 M5 9 v14\" stroke=\"#2f3a2b\" stroke-width=\"3\"/></g>\n<text x=\"218\" y=\"240\" font-size=\"15\" font-weight=\"bold\" fill=\"#2f3a2b\">you</text>\n<g><path d=\"M30 196 v44 m-8 -12 l8 12 l8 -12\" fill=\"none\" stroke=\"#4a7fb0\" stroke-width=\"4\" stroke-linecap=\"round\" stroke-linejoin=\"round\"/><animateTransform attributeName=\"transform\" type=\"rotate\" values=\"0 30 220;0 30 220;180 30 220;180 30 220\" keyTimes=\"0;0.55;0.8;1\" dur=\"7s\" fill=\"freeze\"/></g><g><path d=\"M370 196 v44 m-8 -12 l8 12 l8 -12\" fill=\"none\" stroke=\"#4a7fb0\" stroke-width=\"4\" stroke-linecap=\"round\" stroke-linejoin=\"round\"/><animateTransform attributeName=\"transform\" type=\"rotate\" values=\"0 370 220;0 370 220;180 370 220;180 370 220\" keyTimes=\"0;0.55;0.8;1\" dur=\"7s\" fill=\"freeze\"/></g>\n<text x=\"30\" y=\"270\" font-size=\"15\" font-weight=\"bold\" fill=\"#4a7fb0\" text-anchor=\"middle\">wind</text><text x=\"370\" y=\"270\" font-size=\"15\" font-weight=\"bold\" fill=\"#4a7fb0\" text-anchor=\"middle\">wind</text>\n<g><text x=\"200\" y=\"322\" font-size=\"17\" font-weight=\"bold\" fill=\"#4a7fb0\" text-anchor=\"middle\">Wind: bear to you. Good.</text><animate attributeName=\"opacity\" values=\"1;1;0\" keyTimes=\"0;0.5;0.6\" dur=\"7s\" fill=\"freeze\"/></g>\n<g opacity=\"0\"><rect x=\"60\" y=\"300\" width=\"280\" height=\"34\" rx=\"8\" fill=\"#e8590c\"/><text x=\"200\" y=\"323\" font-size=\"17\" font-weight=\"bold\" fill=\"#fffaf0\" text-anchor=\"middle\">Wind swung. Bear smells you.</text><animate attributeName=\"opacity\" values=\"0;1\" begin=\"6s\" dur=\"0.5s\" fill=\"freeze\"/></g>\n</svg>\n<figcaption>One whiff and a pressured bear goes nocturnal. <button class=\"anim-replay\">↻ Replay</button></figcaption></figure><ul><li>Bears near people feed more at night <span class=\"cert c-lo\" title=\"Certainty\">75%</span>.</li><li>Bumped bears come back after dark, if at all (Tip).</li></ul><details class=\"more\"><summary>More: pressure in detail</summary><ul><li>WildSafeBC: bears are mainly diurnal \"but may feed at night in high risk, human active areas\" <span class=\"cert c-lo\" title=\"Certainty\">75%</span>.</li><li>Massachusetts GPS (Global Positioning System) collars on 86 bears: in developed areas bears moved their foraging to night (65%, secondary write up).</li><li>A road hunted cutblock sees the most pressure. Walk past the gate or glass across the valley (Tip).</li><li>Do not walk through the same patch every evening; glass it from far away (Tip).</li><li>Spring bear hunters crowd the first green road edges; the far side of the valley gets less traffic (Tip).</li></ul></details>","<div class=\"tbl\"><table><thead><tr><th>Time</th><th>Plan (Tip)</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td>1 hour before sunrise</td><td>On a glassing knob before light</td></tr><tr><td>Sunrise to 9:00</td><td>Glass berry slopes and cutblock edges</td></tr><tr><td>9:00 to 15:00</td><td>Scout sign, hang trail cameras, check the wind</td></tr><tr><td>15:00 to sunset</td><td>Back on glass over the best food</td></tr><tr><td>Last light</td><td>Stay until 1 hour after sunset, then out safely</td></tr></tbody></table></div><ul><li>Legal hours are the frame; the bear decides inside it (Tip).</li><li>Plan with the <a href=\"#/plan\">planner</a> and the <a href=\"#/s/local-heffley\">Heffley Creek</a> page.</li></ul>","<figure class=\"diagram\"><svg xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/2000/svg\" viewBox=\"0 0 400 300\" font-family=\"sans-serif\" role=\"img\" aria-label=\"24 hour clock of a typical fall black bear day. Feeding peaks at dawn and dusk, shown in orange, about 6 to 8:30 in the morning and 4:30 to 7:30 in the evening. Through the day it feeds and beds in shade, shown in sage. Night is mostly rest, but near people bears feed more at night. Times are typical, not exact.\">\n<rect x=\"0\" y=\"0\" width=\"400\" height=\"300\" fill=\"#fffaf0\"/>\n<text x=\"200\" y=\"24\" font-size=\"17\" font-weight=\"bold\" fill=\"#23261f\" text-anchor=\"middle\">A fall bear day (typical)</text><circle cx=\"200\" cy=\"156\" r=\"100\" fill=\"#dfe6d3\"/><path d=\"M107.6 117.7 A100 100 0 0 1 300.0 156.0 L270.0 156.0 A70 70 0 0 0 135.3 129.2 Z\" fill=\"#3d4a5c\"/><path d=\"M300.0 156.0 A100 100 0 0 1 279.3 216.9 L255.5 198.6 A70 70 0 0 0 270.0 156.0 Z\" fill=\"#e8590c\"/><path d=\"M279.3 216.9 A100 100 0 0 1 107.6 194.3 L135.3 182.8 A70 70 0 0 0 255.5 198.6 Z\" fill=\"#8a9a6b\"/><path d=\"M107.6 194.3 A100 100 0 0 1 107.6 117.7 L135.3 129.2 A70 70 0 0 0 135.3 182.8 Z\" fill=\"#e8590c\"/><text x=\"200.0\" y=\"47.0\" font-size=\"14\" font-weight=\"bold\" fill=\"#23261f\" text-anchor=\"middle\">0</text><text x=\"280.61017305526644\" y=\"80.38982694473358\" font-size=\"14\" font-weight=\"bold\" fill=\"#23261f\" text-anchor=\"middle\">3</text><text x=\"314.0\" y=\"161.0\" font-size=\"14\" font-weight=\"bold\" fill=\"#23261f\" text-anchor=\"middle\">6</text><text x=\"280.61017305526644\" y=\"241.61017305526642\" font-size=\"14\" font-weight=\"bold\" fill=\"#23261f\" text-anchor=\"middle\">9</text><text x=\"200.0\" y=\"275.0\" font-size=\"14\" font-weight=\"bold\" fill=\"#23261f\" text-anchor=\"middle\">12</text><text x=\"119.38982694473358\" y=\"241.61017305526644\" font-size=\"14\" font-weight=\"bold\" fill=\"#23261f\" text-anchor=\"middle\">15</text><text x=\"86.0\" y=\"161.0\" font-size=\"14\" font-weight=\"bold\" fill=\"#23261f\" text-anchor=\"middle\">18</text><text x=\"119.38982694473357\" y=\"80.38982694473358\" font-size=\"14\" font-weight=\"bold\" fill=\"#23261f\" text-anchor=\"middle\">21</text><circle cx=\"200\" cy=\"156\" r=\"70\" fill=\"#fffaf0\"/><text x=\"200\" y=\"132\" font-size=\"14\" fill=\"#23261f\" text-anchor=\"middle\">Orange: feeding</text><text x=\"200\" y=\"149\" font-size=\"14\" fill=\"#23261f\" text-anchor=\"middle\">peaks dawn, dusk</text><text x=\"200\" y=\"166\" font-size=\"14\" fill=\"#23261f\" text-anchor=\"middle\">Sage: feeds</text><text x=\"200\" y=\"183\" font-size=\"14\" fill=\"#23261f\" text-anchor=\"middle\">and beds in shade</text><text x=\"200\" y=\"294\" font-size=\"14\" font-weight=\"bold\" fill=\"#2f3a2b\" text-anchor=\"middle\">Near people: more feeding at night (75%)</text>\n</svg>\n</figure><ul><li><strong>Rhyme:</strong> \"First light, last light, bears are in sight.\"</li><li><strong>Number trick:</strong> 1 and 1: hunt 1 hour before sunrise to 1 hour after sunset <span class=\"cert c-hi\" title=\"Certainty\">99%</span>.</li><li><strong>Old hand's rule</strong> (opinion, Jim Shockey via Boone and Crockett): \"The big bear holds the best food at the best time.\"</li></ul><details class=\"more\"><summary>More: more hooks</summary><ul><li><strong>Number trick:</strong> 20: up to about 20 hours a day of fall foraging <span class=\"cert c-lo\" title=\"Certainty\">65%</span>.</li><li><strong>Rhyme:</strong> \"Hot noon, shady bed; cool day, longer spread.\"</li><li><strong>Tip:</strong> glass the far side, not the road side.</li></ul><aside class=\"callout mistake\"><div class=\"callout-t\">Common mistakes</div><ul><li>Leaving the glass at 9:00 in October, when bears feed longer in cool weather.</li><li>Driving the same road every evening.</li><li>Believing moon rules for bears with no data.</li></ul></aside><aside class=\"callout field\"><div class=\"callout-t\">Do this in the field</div><p>Pick one cutblock. Glass it at dawn, noon and dusk on one day and log every bear in the Journal.</p></aside></details>","<ul><li>WildSafeBC, <a href=\"https://wildsafebc.com/species/black-bear/\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">Black bear</a>, checked 2026-10-11 <span class=\"cert c-lo\" title=\"Certainty\">75%</span></li><li>BC Ministry of Environment, Lands and Parks (2001), <a href=\"https://www.env.gov.bc.ca/wld/documents/blackbear.pdf\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">\"Black Bears in British Columbia\"</a>, read directly, checked 2026-10-11 <span class=\"cert c-mid\" title=\"Certainty\">90%</span></li><li>Geography Realm, <a href=\"https://www.geographyrealm.com/gps-tracking-shows-that-black-bears-avoid-humans-during-the-day/\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">GPS (Global Positioning System) tracking shows black bears avoid humans during the day</a> (Massachusetts study of 86 bears), search preview, checked 2026-10-11 <span class=\"cert c-lo\" title=\"Certainty\">65%</span></li><li>Hyperphagia foraging hours: town and agency pages (Lake Lure, North Carolina Wildlife Resources Commission via WLOS television news), search preview, checked 2026-10-11 <span class=\"cert c-lo\" title=\"Certainty\">65%</span></li><li>BC Hunting and Trapping Regulations Synopsis 2026 to 2028, via <a href=\"#/s/rb-legal-methods\">legal methods</a>: page 11 <span class=\"cert c-hi\" title=\"Certainty\">99%</span></li><li>Research notes: <code>research/2026-10-11-masterclass-black-bear.md</code>.</li></ul>"]